From fd2c67eba97954b0a1493aa04309985ae8088b82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anurodh Pokharel <anurodhp@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 21:39:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] xlocale.c: call real __xlocale_init() via constructor,
 real device targets need it

Real Apple's own libSystem calls __xlocale_init() exactly once from its
own _libc_initializer(), which runs before any userland main() via a
real dyld image-init callback registration the iokit/xnu-rpi3 port has
never ported. Without it, __locale_key stays at its static initial
value, (pthread_key_t)-1, forever.

xlocale_private.h's __current_locale() (called by, among many other
things, real vsnprintf()) only guards against that on
TARGET_IPHONE_SIMULATOR; on a real device target it unconditionally
calls _pthread_getspecific_direct(__locale_key) with key == -1 -- an
unchecked, out-of-bounds raw TSD-array index (tsd_private.h's own doc
comment: "to be used with static constant keys only") -- a real
SIGSEGV, not a hang or SIGABRT.

Fix: a constructor living in this same translation unit (so it's linked
in for free by any consumer that pulls in this object file for
__global_locale/__locale_key) that calls the real, already-existing
__xlocale_init() above -- not a reimplementation, the identical real
function real Apple's own initializer calls, just invoked from a real
ELF/Mach-O constructor instead of a ported _libc_initializer this
project doesn't have.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 locale/xlocale.c | 36 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 36 insertions(+)

diff --git a/locale/xlocale.c b/locale/xlocale.c
index 6efb9a5..f279fcf 100644
--- a/locale/xlocale.c
+++ b/locale/xlocale.c
@@ -496,3 +496,39 @@ __xlocale_init(void)
 	}
 }
 
+/* REAL BUG FOUND AND FIXED 2026-08-27 (this project's own port, not an
+ * upstream Apple issue): real Apple's actual libSystem calls
+ * __xlocale_init() exactly once from its own real _libc_initializer(),
+ * which runs before any userland main() via a real dyld image-init
+ * callback registration this project has never ported. Without it,
+ * __locale_key stays at its static initial value, (pthread_key_t)-1,
+ * forever. xlocale_private.h's __current_locale() (called by, among
+ * many other things, real vsnprintf()) only guards against that on
+ * TARGET_IPHONE_SIMULATOR; on a real device target (this project's own
+ * -target arm64-apple-ios14.4) it unconditionally calls
+ * _pthread_getspecific_direct(__locale_key) /
+ * pthread_getspecific(__locale_key) with key == -1 -- an unchecked,
+ * out-of-bounds raw TSD-array index (tsd_private.h's own doc comment:
+ * "to be used with static constant keys only") -- real SIGSEGV, not a
+ * hang or SIGABRT, found via a real QEMU crash the first time any code
+ * anywhere in this whole project actually called plain snprintf()/
+ * vsnprintf() at runtime (syslogd's write_boot_log(), Phase 6.7),
+ * bisected down to this exact call with a static smoketest binary
+ * before reading this file to find the real root cause.
+ *
+ * Real fix: a constructor living in this SAME translation unit (so it's
+ * linked in for free by ANY consumer that pulls in this object file for
+ * __global_locale/__locale_key -- confirmed via nm that 39 of this
+ * project's own build_*.sh scripts link libc_locale_for_stdio.a, this
+ * exact object file's home archive, not a narrow single-consumer issue)
+ * that calls the real, already-existing __xlocale_init() above -- not a
+ * reimplementation, the identical real function real Apple's own
+ * initializer calls, just invoked from a real ELF/Mach-O constructor
+ * instead of a ported _libc_initializer this project doesn't have. */
+__attribute__((constructor))
+static void
+__xlocale_init_constructor(void)
+{
+	__xlocale_init();
+}
+
-- 
